WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:07.920
So we didn’t have company every night, but we had company at least one night a week.

2
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.160
And all cloth napkins.

3
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.620
All linen tablecloths.

4
00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:22.140
All china; the china’s still in the Human Ecology building that was in the home management houses.

5
00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:28.760
And there was silver to be polished and . . . you know, there were a lot of little chores to be done.

6
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:33.640
And I remember, it was not my job when I moved out of the home management house,

7
00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:43.440
I helped Miss [?] . . . it was not my job to take care of the linens that week or that last . . . but I was the last one in the house.

8
00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:51.440
So I remember the professor telling me before I left, “You need to mend those linens before you leave.”

9
00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.660
And I said, I thought, “But that was not my job.”

10
00:00:55.660 --> 00:01:01.613
I always felt put upon because I had to stop and mend those linens before I could leave the home management house. [laughs]
